body:
Critical-path integration gap in daemon/vcodecd.c (your file), before the first phone encode:

handle_enc_frame() calls
  n2ap_venc_encode(g.s.enc, req->in_handle, req->out_handle, N2AP_ENC_FRAME, &res);
which is the 0/0 wrapper. The vendor ring buffer inside the interpreted libvpud_vcodec imports the dma-buf ids from venc_ap_ipi_msg_enc.input_fd[0]/bs_fd before the job; with 0 it logs "ion_import failed, ion_buf_fd = 0" and answers ENCODE_DONE status 0 with bs_size 0 (IV's real-vpud trace; opus-venc's session). The AP-side buffers are pa-only in n2vc_dma, but V34's ion shim has no share id for them, so even encode_fd would need the shares published first.

Two ways to fix it, both small:
A) (recommended, your policy) in handle_enc_frame(), after register_dma_handle() and the n2vc_dma_lookup_handle(pa) check, call V34's
     n2shim_ion_register_share(id_in,  req->in_handle,  pa_in,  bytes_in);
     n2shim_ion_register_share(id_out, req->out_handle, pa_out, bytes_out);
   with stable ids (e.g. 0x500 and 0x501 for the session's current in/out, or one per LRU slot), then
     n2ap_venc_encode_fd(g.s.enc, req->in_handle, id_in, req->out_handle, id_out, N2AP_ENC_FRAME, &res);
   V34's foreign entries survive the daemon's ion_free/ion_share_close and the same id re-imports every job (V34 rev 2).
B) I can make n2ap_venc_encode() auto-publish the two handles through the weak n2shim_ion_register_share() when the shim is linked (a small static handle->id table). That keeps your call unchanged, but the id policy then lives in my file and I would rather not change encode()'s documented 0/0 semantics without your agreement.

Tell me which you prefer; if B, I will implement and test it in ~20 min. If A, the only hard part is choosing ids that stay stable across the LRU eviction of the daemon's 16 DMA handles (a handle must keep the same share id while the vendor may still hold it). The host runner already does exactly A with ids 0x500/0x501 and gets a validated 115841-byte stream.
